/-!
# A finite coordinate space for the exterior restriction

The columns below are a proposed basis of im(A - 1), with chosen lifts and
dual rows. The 125 displayed matrices define a candidate linear space for
the induced action. These definitions do not assert that an arbitrary
exterior stabilizer belongs to that space.

The intended proof has two separate steps: place the induced matrix in this
space using mixed evaluations, and use orthogonality and nine restricted
exterior forms to derive the nine chart quadrics. Numerical discovery of
these steps remains to be certified. See source/README.md for conventions,
provenance, and the exact finite contracts.
-/

